---

* **Summary:**

RTL-Level PPA Optimization focuses on improving **Power, Performance, and Area** through better architecture and RTL implementation decisions.

Important techniques include reducing logic depth, selecting appropriate data widths, controlling switching activity, optimizing pipelines, sharing hardware when appropriate, reducing unnecessary registers and multiplexers, managing fanout, and choosing efficient arithmetic and memory architectures.

The most important principle is:

> **Do not optimize RTL blindly. Identify the real PPA bottleneck, make a controlled change, verify functionality, and measure the implementation result.**

